From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: no AI Mode, and Safe Browsing off by default

What Chrome sent to Google with no one signed in (a net-export log at the
sign-in screen, each request traced by its traffic annotation):

- aim_eligibility_fetch: the omnibox's AI Mode asked www.google.com
  whether this user may use it, at every start; reading the sign-in cookie
  jar for that, it also asked accounts.google.com (gaia_auth_list_accounts).
  AI Mode is off (kAimEnabled), so neither is sent.
- safe_browsing_v4_update: Safe Browsing fetched its lists from
  safebrowsing.googleapis.com, which refuses them without Google's API
  keys, which NickelOS doesn't have: it protected nothing. Off by default;
  Settings still shows the choice (and says there is no protection).

The component updater (update.googleapis.com) stays: it brings security
data such as the certificate revocation list.

diff --git a/components/omnibox/browser/aim_eligibility_service_features.cc b/components/omnibox/browser/aim_eligibility_service_features.cc
index c23cef8903ea8..1859914b9de4c 100644
--- a/components/omnibox/browser/aim_eligibility_service_features.cc
+++ b/components/omnibox/browser/aim_eligibility_service_features.cc
@@ -8,7 +8,9 @@
 
 namespace omnibox {
 
-BASE_FEATURE(kAimEnabled, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+// NickelOS: no AI Mode. Its eligibility service asked www.google.com at every
+// start (and, through the sign-in cookie jar, accounts.google.com).
+BASE_FEATURE(kAimEnabled, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 BASE_FEATURE(kAimServerEligibilityEnabled, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
diff --git a/components/safe_browsing/core/common/safe_browsing_prefs.cc b/components/safe_browsing/core/common/safe_browsing_prefs.cc
index ed4747e5ffc10..3ea8fd16d82db 100644
--- a/components/safe_browsing/core/common/safe_browsing_prefs.cc
+++ b/components/safe_browsing/core/common/safe_browsing_prefs.cc
@@ -275,8 +275,11 @@ void RegisterProfilePrefs(PrefRegistrySimple* registry) {
       prefs::kSafeBrowsingEsbProtegoPingWithTokenLastLogTime, base::Time());
   registry->RegisterTimePref(
       prefs::kSafeBrowsingEsbProtegoPingWithoutTokenLastLogTime, base::Time());
+  // NickelOS: off by default. Safe Browsing needs Google's API keys, which
+  // NickelOS doesn't have: on, it protected nothing and only fetched lists
+  // from safebrowsing.googleapis.com, which refused them.
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
-      prefs::kSafeBrowsingEnabled, true,
+      prefs::kSafeBrowsingEnabled, false,
       user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable::SYNCABLE_PREF);
   if (base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kEsbAsASyncedSetting)) {
     registry->RegisterBooleanPref(
